# UI spec

The written design spec the ui-loop reviewers judge every screen against. Keep
it short and decidable: a reviewer must be able to say "met" or "not met" from
a screenshot plus its lint numbers. Owner decisions are logged at the end and
never re-litigated.

## Principles

- One painter per background: a surface is drawn once; a region inside a card
  is a section divided by a hairline and space, never a second card.
- Every count and its name are one object; an empty state says what to do next.
- Text never clips mid-glyph; truncation is deliberate and has the full text
  one hover or tap away.

## Tokens and grid

- Spacing, control heights and icon sizes sit on the {{.Grid}}px grid.
- Touch targets are at least {{.TouchTarget}}×{{.TouchTarget}}px on coarse pointers.
- Colours come from tokens only; text meets WCAG AA in both themes.

